From 28a8ea85cdecc62ec2f66e54ff86f71587722b53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:57:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 69/73] apps: Gives the graph DockApps preferences: Themes,
 style, label, click.

wlm_graph_shared reads the preferences file of wlmcpugraph, wlmmemgraph and
wlmnetgraph, watches it, and applies changes right away, clearing the graph:
- Theme: The shared color themes (a gradient, line and background), or the
  graph's own colors.
- Interval: Seconds between updates; --interval remains the default.
- GraphStyle: Filled, or just the line.
- ShowLabel: Whether to show the label.
- ClickCommand: Runs on a left click, eg. a task manager.
The label may have several lines. A graph of a single value is colored by
height, like a level meter.

And their own:
- wlmcpugraph: Cores (each core's usage, or the total), and a label with the
  total usage in percent, hidden by default.
- wlmmemgraph: Units (MB/GB, or percent), ShowSwap (a second line).
- wlmnetgraph: Interface (all, or one), Label (the scale, or the download
  and upload rates), Units (bytes, or bits per second).
